I have long been fond of the simple reality-based innoculation
proposed by Freeman Dyson. (Reality seems to be a good cure
for a lot of stupid memes.)

His argument: consider the relative difficulty of getting
something out of your local government, out of your state
government, and out of your national government. Consider how
often your national government does things you find
reprehensible, because it's responding to pressures that have
nothing at all to do with your values. Now, explain with a
straight face how you think a world government would _really_
be an improvement.

I've found it very good for at least slowing down
world-government rants, and in at least one case the ranter
did eventually go on to end up an anarchist. He just hadn't
giiven sufficient thought to the problems of a world
government run by anyone now living, as opposed to some ideal
humanity.


